<title>GERMANY: Springer sees notable profit rise in 97.</title>
<headline>Springer sees notable profit rise in 97.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>German publishing group Axel Springer, publisher of the mass circulation Bild, said on Friday that it expects a notable improvement in profit in the 1997 business year.</p>
<p>The group made the statement while releasing its 1996 annual report.</p>
<p>Several weeks ago the group had already reported an increase in 1996 net profits to 163.8 million marks and said it would raise the dividend to 20 marks from 14 marks.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, + 49 69 756525</p>
